msgid "Kashida Color Library Help"
msgstr ""

msgid "Guide to managing color groups, entering and importing color data, defining a custom attribute for each group, preparing the color table, and using the Shortcode to display colors on your website."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Create a Group"
msgstr ""

msgid "Open Kashida Color Library → Add Group."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enter the group name and optionally add a description and featured image."
msgstr ""

msgid "Save the group; a fixed code such as KCS-0001 will be generated automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "The group code does not depend on the group name and does not change when the name changes. It is used in the Shortcode and URL."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Add Colors Manually"
msgstr ""

msgid "Open the required group."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the Color Group box, click Add New Color."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enter the color name, code, HEX value, optional attribute value, and sample image if needed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Save the group."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. Import Colors and Supporting Files"
msgstr ""

msgid "Colors can be imported from CSV or XLSX, and ZIP can be used when sample images need to be included with the data file."
